BROWSER ACCEPTANCE — ATTEMPT 2 (parent-run managed browser)
Circuit: STUDIO SECURITY + BROWSER ACCEPTANCE, PR #255 addendum.
Date: 2026-11-03, 13:31-13:33 CST (harness-measured run window).
Server: gui.server from PR #255 final head c3d32543f5b0604c2e70a84ab32b2a2567a855d3,
owner BrowserAccept, bound 127.0.0.1:8791 on this VM.
Server reachability from the VM itself: VERIFIED — GET / returned 200 and
GET /api/dells returned the 100-Dell registry immediately before the attempt;
server confirmed still listening (200) after the attempt, then stopped by PID.

Attempt: the parent agent delegated a genuine UI drive to the harness-managed
browser (load page; count Dell Rack entries; load an example seed; click Run;
read canvas outcome classes and console errors).

RESULT: NOT PERFORMED — environment boundary, mechanism identified:
- Direct navigation to http://127.0.0.1:8791/ and http://localhost:8791/ was
  rejected by the browser tool as invalid_request before any network access.
- Loopback-resolving public hostnames for the same port (lvh.me,
  127.0.0.1.nip.io) loaded the browser's own error page:
  ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED.
- A public site (example.com) loaded normally in the same session, so the
  browser itself was functional.
Conclusion: the managed browser runs in a network environment that does not
share this VM's loopback; nothing was listening on port 8791 *in the
browser's environment*, while the server verifiably listened on the VM's.

Steps 2-6 of the acceptance drive (rack count, example load, Run click,
canvas verdicts, console errors) were therefore NOT performed and remain
UNVERIFIED. No JavaScript errors from the app were observed (the app never
loaded). Real-browser acceptance remains OUTSTANDING after two documented,
mechanistically distinct blocked routes (direct-launch policy refusal;
managed-browser loopback isolation). Remaining routes: a human opening the
Studio in their own browser (a genuine REAL_USER_PATH check), or a future
environment with a launchable Chromium for the preserved CDP driver
(browser_acceptance.py).
